WHY `UNKNOWN` IS NOT `UNSUPPORTED`
`src/focusrite-client.js` clears its state cache at device arrival, seeds only values explicitly supplied by the server in the device-arrival payload, then updates the cache from subsequent `<set>` messages. `getValue()` only returns that cache. There is currently no per-item read/query command in the module. Missing values are intentionally left unknown rather than defaulted.

Therefore `BASELINE_UNKNOWN` means `not observed in this client session`, not `schema item absent` and not `hardware capability absent`.

